-- The Hall of Paintings (the book's Area 1 map, 4A-4K), redrawn in our pieces and turned so north is
-- up. The book's arrangement: the door in from the entrance chamber at the south-west, where the
-- entrance takes a corner out of the hall; the cut north-west and north-east corners; the slanting
-- south-east wall with the door on to the gift shop; paintings all along the walls. Paintings the
-- book hangs on slanting walls sit in little straight stretches of wall here, in the book's
-- order round the room. The two on the south wall (the DM's side, left off) moved: the duellist
-- to the slanting wall, and the knight's portrait to the far (east) end, as the book's text has
-- it, behind a red rope.

